The filesystem sandbox helper parent currently writes the helper request,
closes stdin, and then waits for child output through wait_with_output(). On
Solaris we have observed the helper process sleeping in write(1) with a large
JSON response while the parent remains alive, which can wedge apply_patch and
other filesystem helper requests.

Start draining the helper stdout and stderr pipes before waiting for the child.
This keeps large helper responses from filling the pipe and blocking the helper
before it can exit. Add a regression test that returns a helper-shaped response
larger than a typical pipe buffer.

